userStories.description:
**Goal** — Replace O(n) full re-import with incremental diff-and-apply against durable graph tables.

**Motivation** — importGraphify() deletes all nodes then re-indexes everything in memory, causing timeouts at 500+ nodes.

**Approach** — 5-step diff algorithm: (1) load stored graph from GraphNode + GraphLink tables, (2) compute added/updated/removed sets by comparing incoming nodes with stored nodes, (3) delete removed nodes from both Prisma and LanceDB, (4) upsert added/updated nodes to Prisma and regenerate adjacency text for changed nodes only, (5) upsert only changed nodes into LanceDB vector store. Skip re-indexing nodes whose label, type, source_file, and outgoing links are unchanged.

**Interface**
```typescript
class IncrementalGraphDiffService {
  async diffAndApply(
    projectId: string,
    newNodes: GraphifyNodeDto[],
    newLinks: GraphifyLinkDto[],
  ): Promise<DiffResult>

  async getStoredGraph(projectId: string): Promise<StoredGraph>
}

interface StoredGraph {
  nodeMap: Map<string, GraphifyNodeDto>;
  linkMap: Map<string, GraphifyLinkDto[]>;
}

interface DiffResult {
  added: number;
  updated: number;
  removed: number;
  indexed: number;  // total nodes re-indexed into vector store
  durationMs: number;
}
```

**Scope** — In: existing importGraphify endpoint and RagService, graphify adjacency graph. Out: IncrementalGraphDiffService, GraphNode/GraphLink Prisma tables, modified RagService.importGraphify() to use diff-and-apply.

**Goal** — Extract symbol-level metadata from source files and store in durable Symbol table.

**Motivation** — Adjacency text is not true symbol-level metadata; need deterministic, parser-based extraction of symbols, signatures, and call graphs.

**Approach** — Parse TypeScript/JavaScript source files with ts-morph to extract symbol metadata: name, kind (class/method/function/interface/enum), location (file, startLine, endLine), signature (parameter types + return type), and call graph (callers, callees). Store in Symbol table with unique symbolId = '{repoId}:{filePath}::{SymbolName}'. Process only files changed in the commit (incremental). Validate that all symbol IDs, locations, and call graph entries are parser-derived, not LLM-inferred. Push webhook handlers must resolve file contents before calling AstIndexService.indexCommit().

**Interface**
```typescript
class AstIndexService {
  async indexCommit(
    repoId: string,
    commitHash: string,
    files: SourceFile[],
  ): Promise<SymbolIndexResult>

  async getSymbol(projectId: string, symbolId: string): Promise<Symbol | null>

  async getCallers(projectId: string, symbolId: string): Promise<CallerInfo[]>

  async getCallees(projectId: string, symbolId: string): Promise<CalleeInfo[]>
}

interface SourceFile {
  path: string;     // relative path
  content: string;  // full source code
}

interface SymbolIndexResult {
  commitHash: string;
  symbolsIndexed: number;
  filesIndexed: number;
  fileErrors: Array<{ path: string; error: string }>;
  durationMs: number;
}

interface Symbol {
  id: string;         // database ID
  symbolId: string;   // '{repoId}:{filePath}::{SymbolName}'
  projectId: string;
  repoId: string;
  commitHash: string;
  name: string;       // 'AuthService.login'
  kind: 'class' | 'method' | 'function' | 'interface' | 'enum';
  file: string;       // relative path
  startLine: number;
  endLine: number;
  signature?: string; // parameter types + return type
  callers: string[];  // symbol IDs of functions that call this
  callees: string[];  // symbol IDs of functions this calls
  docComment?: string;
}
```

**Scope** — In: source file contents from VCS webhooks, existing Prisma infrastructure. Out: AstIndexService, Symbol Prisma table, call graph metadata, symbol lookup APIs.

**Goal** — Build durable ticket/service/owner entity graph linked to code graph.

**Motivation** — Code graph is isolated from operational context; need to link tickets to services to code to analyze incident impact.

**Approach** — Create EntityNode and EntityLink Prisma tables to persistently store entity graph. Entity types: ticket (from TicketEvent), service (from graphify nodes with type=code_module), owner (from ticket assignedToUserId/assignedToAgentId), incident (from tickets with priority=critical|high). Link creation: ticket→service from gitRefFile/labels/graphified source_file, ticket→owner from assignedToUserId/assignedToAgentId, service→service from graphify links with relation=depends_on, incident→ticket from linking events. Implement incremental updates via outbox fan-out: onTicketEvent, onGraphifyImport. Support graph traversal: getRelatedEntities(depth), getIncidentImpact(). All entity graph data is durable; do not depend on Phase 2's in-memory EntityStore for impact analysis.

**Interface**
```typescript
class EntityGraphService {
  async rebuildGraph(projectId: string): Promise<void>

  async onTicketEvent(event: TicketEvent): Promise<void>
  async onGraphifyImport(projectId: string, nodes: GraphifyNodeDto[]): Promise<void>

  async getRelatedEntities(projectId: string, entityId: string, depth?: number): Promise<EntityPath[]>

  async getIncidentImpact(projectId: string, incidentTicketId: string): Promise<ImpactAnalysis>
}

interface EntityPath {
  path: EntityRecord[];
  relation: string;
  depth: number;
}

interface ImpactAnalysis {
  incidentTicketId: string;
  affectedServices: EntityRecord[];
  affectedTickets: EntityRecord[];
  affectedCodeModules: EntityRecord[];
  rootCause?: string;
}

interface EntityRecord {
  id: string;
  entityId: string;
  type: string;
  label: string;
  tags: string[];
}
```

**Scope** — In: existing Ticket, TicketEvent models; graphify nodes; Phase 2 entity relationships. Out: EntityNode/EntityLink Prisma tables, EntityGraphService with traversal APIs, incremental update hooks.

**Goal** — Query API that analyzes impact of code changes across symbols, services, and tickets.

**Motivation** — Agents need to understand which operational entities are affected by a code change before deciding on deployment, rollback, or escalation.

**Approach** — Implement ImpactAnalysisService that composes Symbol, GraphNode, and EntityNode queries. For a given commit + changed files, find: (1) impacted symbols from Symbol table where file matches changedFiles, (2) impacted services linked to symbols via GraphNode.sourceFile → EntityNode.sourceId, (3) impacted tickets linked to services via EntityLink, (4) compute impactScore from formula: 0.3 * (affectedSymbols / totalSymbols * 100) + 0.3 * (affectedServices / totalServices * 100) + 0.2 * (affectedTickets / totalTickets * 100) + 0.2 * (linkedIncidents > 0 ? 100 : 0), clamped to [0, 100]. If any denominator is zero, that term contributes 0. Include provenance metadata. Expose via GET /projects/:slug/codeintel/impact?repoId=X&commitHash=Y&changedFiles=file1,file2.

**Interface**
```typescript
class ImpactAnalysisService {
  async getChangeImpact(query: ChangeImpactQuery): Promise<ChangeImpactResult>
}

interface ChangeImpactQuery {
  projectId: string;
  repoId: string;
  commitHash: string;
  changedFiles: string[];
  ticketId?: string;  // optional: tie to a ticket
}

interface ChangeImpactResult {
  commitHash: string;
  changedFiles: string[];
  impactedSymbols: Symbol[];
  impactedServices: EntityRecord[];
  impactedTickets: EntityRecord[];
  impactScore: number;  // 0-100, composite
  provenance: Provenance;
}

interface Provenance {
  query: ChangeImpactQuery;
  sources: { [key: string]: string };  // e.g. { symbolIndex: 'Symbol table', entityGraph: 'EntityNode/EntityLink' }
  computedAt: Date;
}
```

**Scope** — In: Symbol, GraphNode, EntityNode tables; existing project and repo models. Out: ImpactAnalysisService, impact API endpoint, impact score formula implementation.

**Goal** — Provide a single canonical read path for authoritative project state (tickets, events, decisions).

**Motivation** — Multiple services may query tickets, events, and decisions; need a single source of truth to prevent inconsistencies and enable Phase 5 context assembly.

**Approach** — Implement thin CanonicalStateService that queries Ticket, TicketEvent, AgentEvent, DecisionEvent, and MemoryItem (kind=DECISION) models. Return snapshot with optional ticket list, recent events, active decisions, and retrievedAt timestamp. Do not query LanceDB, BM25, entity graph, or derived stores; Prisma-only reads. Support filtering by projectId (required), ticketIds (optional, filters which tickets are returned), actorId (optional), and timeWindow (optional, filters events by createdAt). Throw KodaError on non-existent or unauthorized projectId.

**Interface**
```typescript
class CanonicalStateService {
  async getSnapshot(query: CanonicalSnapshotQuery): Promise<CanonicalSnapshot>
}

interface CanonicalSnapshotQuery {
  projectId: string;
  ticketIds?: string[];   // if absent, returns no tickets
  actorId?: string;
  timeWindow?: { from?: Date; to?: Date };
}

interface CanonicalSnapshot {
  tickets?: Array<{
    id: string;
    title: string;
    status: string;
    priority: string;
    assignedToUserId: string | null;
    assignedToAgentId: string | null;
    createdAt: Date;
    updatedAt: Date;
  }>;
  recentEvents?: Array<{
    id: string;
    eventType: string;
    actorId: string;
    action: string;
    payload: Json;
    createdAt: Date;
  }>;
  activeDecisions?: Array<{
    id: string;
    topic: string;
    decision: string;
    rationale: string | null;
    createdAt: Date;
  }>;
  retrievedAt: Date;
}
```

**Scope** — In: existing Ticket, TicketEvent, AgentEvent, DecisionEvent, MemoryItem models. Out: CanonicalStateService with getSnapshot(), integration point for Phase 5 context assembly.
